Subject: [PATCH 2/4] style(layout): tighten desktop density so more content
 fits per screen

At 1440px the hero filled the whole viewport with a 128px name and every
section carried 208px of top and bottom padding, so a screen showed very
little content.

- .section-padding: 208px -> 112px at >=1024, 176px -> 96px at >=768,
  112px -> 80px on mobile
- .content-container 1180px -> 1280px, .content-container-wide
  1400px -> 1520px
- hero: 100svh -> 86svh, name clamp max 8rem -> 5.75rem (128 -> 92px at
  1440), tagline measure 720px -> 640px
- section headings scaled down ~25% (Projects, About, Experience, Contact)

Page height at 1440x900: 8002px -> 6624px.
